#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Run the installed-candidate release gate against a packaged Omega RC.

OMEGA-DELTA-0185. The Episode 263 gap analysis (section 7, "Installed-candidate
release gate") defines the release matrix: source tests are necessary and
insufficient, so every release row must be observed on a PACKAGED candidate
launched from a CLEAN profile, and every row must leave preserved evidence.
This harness scripts that matrix. It never fabricates a row: a row it can
observe end-to-end is `automated-pass` or `automated-fail`, a row that needs a
human account, interactive provider auth, a second person, or a judgment call
is `owner-assisted-pending` with the exact instruction the owner must follow,
and a row the host refuses (missing screen-recording permission, missing
artifact) is `blocked` with the reason. "Nothing was found" and "nobody
looked" must never read the same.

The candidate is the DMG produced by `script/bundle-omega-rc` together with
its release record. Every receipt this harness writes is bound to the
package digest from that record so evidence cannot be re-attributed to a
different build.

The zero-refusal sweep is anchored to `omega_zero_base::refusal` in
`crates/omega_zero_base/src/omega_zero_base.rs`: every refused action logs one
sentence ("... is not part of Omega, which shows one agent thread and the
controls that operate it.") via `report_refusal` in
`crates/omega/src/omega_zero_base_ui.rs`. A flag-free launch that reaches the
composer without dispatching a single refused action must leave a log with
zero such sentences.

Usage:
    script/omega-release-gate [--dmg PATH] [--release-record PATH]
                              [--output-dir DIR] [--skip-launch]
                              [--launch-settle SECONDS] [--report PATH]
                              [--receipt-copy PATH] [--self-test]

Exit codes: 0 = no automated row failed (owner-assisted rows may remain
pending), 1 = at least one automated row failed, 2 = harness error,
3 = self-test failure.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import datetime
import hashlib
import json
import os
import plistlib
import re
import shutil
import signal
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
